We say a test statistic $\mathcal{T}(G_1,G_2)$ with a threshold $\tau$ succeeds in detection, if the sum of Type I and Type II errors is bounded by $0.05$ as $n\to \infty$:
\begin{align}\label{eq:detection-cretiria}
    \limsup_{n\to \infty}\qth{\mathcal{P}_0(\mathcal{T}\ge\tau)+\mathcal{P}_1(\mathcal{T}< \tau)}\le 0.05.
\end{align}

